<title>SINGAPORE: India tenders to sell Madras low aromatic naphtha.</title>
<headline>India tenders to sell Madras low aromatic naphtha.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Indian Oil Corp (IOC) has issued a tender to sell 27,000-tonnes of low aromatic naphtha (LAN) lifting August 6-8 from Madras on the east coast, industry sources said on Monday.</p>
<p>The tender closes July 24 and is valid for a day.</p>
<p>IOC's last LAN cargo from Madras, lifting July 6-8, was awarded at around $21.00 per tonne below Japanese naphtha spot quotes.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65 870 3086)</p>
</text>
